==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 6~10 seconds<sup>180f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 4~6 seconds<sup>120f~180f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 4~6 seconds<sup>120f~180f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[J.K. Bun Bun]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Mooth]]s spawn, delay 6.67~20 seconds<sup>200f~600f</sup>.
**1 [[Lucky Sloth]] spawns.
**1 [[Lucky Sloth]] spawns.

==Strategy==
[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut]] is a must here, being able to chip off much of J.K. Bun Bun's HP. Lure J.K. Bun Bun to your base, and now you're on a fuse. If the Lucky Sloths join in before J.K. Bun Bun is at a low HP, the two will obliterate your front lines. To beat J.K. Bun Bun, on lower crowns you can just spam meatshields, but on {{4c}}, you'll also need [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun]] to deal that extra bit of damage to keep J.K. Bun Bun away. If you have Talented [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman]], this stage becomes much easier due to her survive ability, but even normal Cameraman can help a lot here, doing chip damage, and acting as a replacement meatshield.

